ovie make no  mistake about that there are going to be  multiple different versions of kang this  was set up very clearly in loki and of  course loki season 2 which is filming  right now is also going to be addressing  king however we don't know which version  but let's start off with ant-man and the  wasp quantum mania version of kang  according to the good old rumor mill  modok is going to be kind of in charge  of kang he's going to be the person that  employs kang so this variant of kang the  conqueror that we are going to be seeing  in ant-man 3 might be a little bit more  tame but here's something that you need  to know about kang the conqueror a lot  of people are worried and are saying  that there's not going to be a better  villain in the mcu from here on out than  thanos thanos was peak villainy and  there's no way to top him however i  disagree i think kang is actually going  to top thanos because you have to think  about who exactly king is and you have  to remember the events that happened in  loki one let's not forget that now there  are going to be many many different  versions of kang evil versions of kang  he who remains who is king the conqueror  even said at the very last episode of  loki if you think i'm evil well wait  till you meet my variants the kang  variants themselves caused the  multiversal war just variants of kang  the conqueror variants of nathaniel  richards which was his original name  kang variants alone not a bunch of  different teams not a bunch of  incursions by doctor strange or any  other member of the illuminati or the  avengers no just kang the conqueror  fighting himself and then one of them he  who remains came out on top and defeated  everybody else then he created the tva  to control everything so then in loki  when loki went to court he said that he  wasn't to blame but it was actually the  avengers that were to blame however the  tva said that that was supposed to  happen the avengers were supposed to do  all of that the avengers were supposed  to go back in time they were supposed to  collect all of the infinity stones from  the past go back to their present time  and defeat thanos the tva made that  clear that means that the tva allowed  the avengers to defeat thanos that means  that the tva allowed thanos to do  everything that he did and who is in  charge of the tva kang now originally it  was he who remains that was in charge of  the tva but now at the end of loki since  the tva has kind of changed it is  actually under a real kang the conqueror  not he who remains not a tame variant of  kang but an evil variant of kang we know  this because where there used to be  three statues of time keepers in the tva  it is now only one statue of king the  conqueror so yes thanos was an amazing  villain and the infinity saga was  fantastic infinity war and in game are  two of the greatest movies of all time  not just marvel movies but of all movies  and i'm not trying to take anything away  from that but kang the conqueror let all  of that happen and now we are dealing  with a villain who can kind of control  time and can multiverse hop so this is  going to be on a way bigger scale but  taking it back to ant-man 3 we're still  probably going to be getting a rather  tame version of kang i do not believe  that this is going to be the kang the  conqueror in fact i don't think there's  ever going to really be a the kang the  conqueror one king until the very end  because keep in mind the multiversal war  between all of the kangs is going to be  actively happening so not only are we  going to be seeing our heroes go up  against kang but we're going to see  different variants of kang go up against  each other i'm guessing that some are  actually going to be good some are going  to be kind of in the middle but some are  going to be absolutely ruthless a great  example of that is of kang ruling the  tva at the end of loki season 1 and then  the fact that kang in ant-man 3 is going  to be working 